Actually get_tile_at_pixel is easier. Let me sample along y=150 from x=180 to x=256 step 8, and y=90 from 150-175.\n\nLet me batch get_tile_at_pixel calls? Each is a separate tool. I can call multiple in one message.\n\nAlso note: this is a live game state from a previous session, mid-1-1 with score 1200. The task says \"1-1 has one Koopa Troopa... it appears as the camera nears it\". So journey continues from x~335 to ~1650. That's a long stretch, ~1300 px. At run speed 1.5-2.5 px/frame, that's ~600-800 frames. With invincibility we can just hold right + jump periodically.\n\nLet me first handle the starman since we're right at the mushroom block. Actually, is the brick row's left ? block here? Let me check tiles.\n\nLet me batch:\n- get_tile_at_pixel(224,148) — the ? block in the brick row\n- get_tile_at_pixel(160,88) — the lone ? block\n- get_tile_at_pixel(192,148) — left end of brick row\n- get_tile_at_pixel(208,148)\n- get_tile_at_pixel(240,148)\n- get_tile_at_pixel(96,148) — the lone block at (96,148) in screenshot? There's a block at screen (96,148) — yes I see a single brown block at (96,148). Hmm.\n\nWait the screenshot shows: a single brown block at screen (96,148) (looks like a used block or brick), a ? block at (160,88), and the brick row at (192-256,144). And a bush at bottom left area screen (30,190), hill (100,170).\n\nHmm, the block at (96,148) is at level x 246. In real SMB 1-1, the first \"coin\" ? block is at x=336 alone, and there's a brick block at x=352? Hmm, actually the layout: object at x=... whatever.\n\nLet me just query.\n\nAlso for starman: better to check $0039 semantics via disassembly. Let me disassemble CPU $D7E0-$D850.\n\nLet me batch several tool calls."}
