t (move left), then run+jump to get speed.\n\nApproach: hold left briefly to back off ~40px, then run right+B and jump just before the pipe.\n\nOr: since we have the star, we still can't pass a solid pipe without jumping.\n\nLet me do: play_input [{left,b,20},{right,b,a,20},{right,b,30}, ...]. Hmm.\n\nActually, simpler: back up with left for ~24 frames (~30px), then hold right+B and jump with A held longer (25 frames) to maximize. The run speed builds over ~20 frames, so by the time he reaches the pipe he'll be running and the jump will be higher.\n\nScript: [{left,b,20}, {right,b,25}, {right,b,a,25}, {right,b,40}] then repeat.\n\nHmm, this is fiddly. Alternative: since $079F star invincibility doesn't help with walls, but I could just... hmm.\n\nWait, actually, maybe the wall is not a pipe but the pipe; and remember Mario can also walk onto the pipe if he jumps at the right moment.\n\nLet me think about distance: Mario stuck at 722; the pipe occupies level 727-772 (from screenshot estimate). After clearing the pipe, he lands on top or beyond.\n\nLet me back up and try a running jump. Use play_input:\n[{left,b,26},{right,b,20},{right,b,a,26},{right,b,30}]\nTotal 102 frames.\n\nThen check position.\n\nActually, I realize the jump needs to start ~20-30px before the wall so he's at full run speed and rising as he reaches it. Let me back off ~40px: left for 20 frames (walk left ~1.5*20=30px, plus accel). Then right for 26 frames to accelerate to full speed and cover the 30px back. Then jump (A) while holding right+B for ~26 frames.\n\nHmm, but the jump must begin before hitting the pipe. If he accelerates for 26 frames he may already hit the pipe. Let me instead: after backing off, jump immediately while holding right+B: the run speed builds during the jump? In SMB, air control lets you accelerate in the air. So a jump from nearly standing can still build horizontal speed mid-air. Starting the jump early (from ~40px away) should let him build speed and clear.\n\nScript: