tity: the RAM enemy array slot 1 is active ($000F+1=1), its type byte $0016+1 = 0 (the Goomba's type is 6) and its state $001E+1 = 0 (normal walking). Goombas visible in the same frame are the 16x24 groups with tiles $70-$73 in palette 7. Corroboration: the enemy-sprite layout table at prgRom 0x6756 holds the entry 69 A5 6A A7 A8 A9, which contains this Koopa's tile set.\nREACH (play-to-reach, no position writes for the walking): fresh World 1-1 (reset_emulator to title, play_input [{start,6},{},60,{start,6},{},90]); write CPU $079F=200 (star invincibility, ~4000 frames, so the Goombas cannot kill Mario while he runs); then hold right+B with an A pulse every ~40 frames (script pattern [{right,b,a} 18 frames, {right,b} 22 frames] repeated). Checkpoints saved with save_state: slot 5 = level x 1015 (camera page 3, TIME 358), slot 6 = level x 1292 (past the first pit), slot 7 = level x 1535. Pit checkpoints: the first wide pit is jumped by running right+B ~30 frames from x 1017 then holding right+B+A 30 frames (cleared it, landed x 1292); the second pit near x 1400 is jumped by running right+B ~26 frames from x 1292 then right+B+A 30 frames. From x 1535 just hold right+B ~35 frames - the Koopa (page 6, x ~1690) walks left into view; a Goomba is killed by the star on the way. WARNING: with star invincibility still lit, running into the Koopa kills it, so stop as soon as it is on screen."}}
