{"type":"text","text":"Done — both metasprites are named and recorded, and promoted into the ROM's mapping file.\n\n## Koopa Troopa (`id: koopa`)\n**Reach (play-to-reach, no position writes for the walking):** fresh World 1-1 (reset → Start, wait, Start), then `$079F`=200 for star invincibility and a run of `right+B` with an A pulse every ~40 frames. Pitches handled by checkpointing: **slot 5** x≈1015, **slot 6** x≈1292 (past the first wide pit; jump = run right+B ~30 frames, then hold right+B+A 30), **slot 7** x≈1535. The second pit (x≈1400) is cleared the same way. From 1535 just held right+B ~35 frames.\n\n**Proof (paused, list_sprites, OAM slots 40-45, origin (187,185), level x≈1692, enemy slot 1 type 0):** 16x24 metasprite, sprite palette 5, all flipped horizontally (walking left):\n- `$A5` (165) (+0,+0) · `$FC` (252, blank) (+8,+0) · `$A7` (167) (+0,+8) · `$A6` (166) (+8,+8) · `$A9` (169) (+0,+16) · `$A8` (168) (+8,+16)\n\n## Starman (`id: starman`)\n**Reach:** in fresh 1-1, jumped into the **left `?` block of the brick row** (level x≈336, the mushroom block). The hit runs CPU `$BC66` (sets `$049F`=3) and stores the item type in `$0039` via the entry-point trick at `$BDD2/$BDD5/$BDD8` (0=mushroom/flower, 2=star, 3=1-up). While the item was still emerging I wrote **`$0039`=2**; the emerging-item handler at `$BC85` reads `$0039` every frame and switched to the star branch, redrawing the sprite with the star tiles.\n\n**Proof (paused, list_sprites, OAM slots 10-13, origin (23,138)):** 16x16 metasprite, sprite palette 6, all behind-background, no vertical flips:\n- `$8D` (141) (+0,+0) · `$8D` flip_h (+8,+0) · `$E4` (228) (+0,+8) · `$E4` flip_h (+8,+8)\n\n`get_region` object mode at (24,143) returned 32 connected palette-6 pixels across OAM #10/#11 (`$8D`), rendered `$27` orange.\n\nTwo things worth noting: the star is drawn *behind* the background, so it only peeks above the block while emerging; and with star invincibility lit, touching the Koopa kills it, so the run has to stop the moment it appears."}
